==============================================================================
S667 embedded maximality order atlas
==============================================================================

Principle
  maximality is not unary: maximal(object, ambient embedding, allowed extensions)
  Q,< is the toy: finite chains have maxima; dense ambient extensions destroy them.

A. Dense-order finite-chain lab
  base_chain=[Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(1, 1), Fraction(2, 1)]
  finite_maximum=2
  one_point_extension_cuts=[('(-infty,0)', Fraction(-1, 1)), ('(0,1)', Fraction(1, 2)), ('(1,2)', Fraction(3, 2)), ('(2,infty)', Fraction(3, 1))]
  ambient_maximum_after_extension=3
  lesson=finite maximality is destroyed by the ambient DLO extension property

B. Dedekind-cut address lab
  cut={q in Q : q^2 < 2}
  finite_denominator_limit=12
  finite_best_lower=7/5
  strictly_better_lower_with_larger_denominator=24/17
  finite_best_square=49/25
  better_square=576/289
  lesson=finite search has a maximum; the embedded Dedekind cut has no rational maximum

C. Same point, different ambient boundary
  point=1
  ambient_maximality={'finite subset {0,1/2,1}': True, 'closed interval [0,1]_Q': True, 'open interval (0,1)_Q': False, 'whole Q': False}
  lesson=the same rational is maximal or not depending on the embedding boundary

D. S666 embedded repair readout
  visible_shadow={'groups': 3, 'mixed': 3, 'max_bucket': 378}
  visible+cheap_pair={'groups': 112, 'mixed': 3, 'max_bucket': 106}
  visible+owner_cover_count={'groups': 976, 'mixed': 2, 'max_bucket': 2}
  visible+owner_private_flag={'groups': 1067, 'mixed': 0, 'max_bucket': 2}
  visible+owner_private_count={'groups': 1134, 'mixed': 0, 'max_bucket': 1}
  lesson=embedded maximality appears when the visible maximum is tested in the owner-deletion ambient

